        '[monthly_letter__Writer__letter_writer__prompt_]:prompt "Writer: letter_writer (prompt)"':
          data:
            enableFunctionCall: false
            promptText: >-
              ## Task: write the monthly letter


              Integrate the analyses below into the client's monthly letter, in
              Brazilian Portuguese. It will be laid out on two A4 pages together
              with two charts and a small results table, so the whole text must
              stay between 380 and 520 words.


              Structure:

              1. greeting with the client's first name;

              2. opening: one or two sentences with the month and the purpose of
              the letter;

              3. performance: the month's result versus CDI and the profile
              benchmark; the most impactful movements, with losses stated
              plainly and, when the analysis links them to the XP scenario, that
              possible explanation; the best performer and the worst performer
              (by return); the top contributor in reais when it is a different
              asset from the best performer, explaining that its weight in the
              portfolio is larger; then the attention points;

              4. macro: how the XP scenario may affect the portfolio;

              5. suggestions: exactly the movements in "Suggestions", same
              order, candidate_id and type copied; each text starts with
              "Discutir com o assessor a possibilidade de..." (or a close
              variation) and never states where the money must go, nor names a
              product or ticker the suggestion does not name;

              6. outlook: what to expect, without promising returns;

              7. closing: availability of the advisor for a conversation.


              Choose the two charts that best support the story, from:
              "allocation" (portfolio by asset class), "contribution"
              (contribution of each asset in R$), "benchmarks" (portfolio vs
              CDI, Ibovespa and profile benchmark).


              Quote figures exactly as they appear in the analyses and attribute
              them only to what they measure (a class return is not the return
              of one fund type or one asset).


              Wording rules (the letter goes to a real client and must follow
              suitability rules):

              - Never state or imply that a movement will improve, increase or
              raise returns, gains or profitability ("pode melhorar a
              rentabilidade", "potencializar ganhos", "aumentar o retorno" are
              not allowed). Describe instead what the movement does to the
              portfolio: diversifies, reduces concentration, adds liquidity,
              aligns the portfolio with the profile, puts idle money to work at
              the CDI rate.

              - XP figures are projections: say "a XP projeta a Selic em 15,50%
              ao fim de 2025" (with the horizon from the digest), never "a Selic
              deve permanecer em". Quote each macro figure once, in the macro
              section; the outlook does not repeat them.

              - Each sentence says what it means grammatically: "incluir renda
              fixa pode trazer proteção", not "a carteira não possui renda fixa,
              o que pode oferecer proteção".

              - Macro effects are conditional and attributed to XP: "o cenário
              projetado pela XP tende a favorecer...", never "vai render".

              - A matured bond is money available to reinvest, not a bad result:
              do not describe it as "sem retorno" or as a concern.

              - Idle cash is "saldo parado sem rendimento"; you may quote its
              opportunity cost in reais, but not promise what it would earn.

              - Address the client as "você" consistently; use correct
              Portuguese ("custo de oportunidade", "ajudá-lo"), and avoid
              starting sentences with "Apesar de" unless a contrast follows in
              the same sentence.


              Each suggestion text keeps the portfolio fact it rests on (e.g.
              "sua carteira não tem renda fixa"), and its title says no more
              than its text. Do not compare a result with an expectation, a
              limit or an ideal that is not in the inputs (no "abaixo do
              esperado", "acima do limite ideal"; the concentration fact gives
              the 15% reference).


              The greeting appears only in greeting_pt. performance_pt has at
              most two paragraphs and each figure is quoted once in the whole
              letter.


              If revision notes are given, fix every issue they list and keep
              the rest, including every suggestion that is grounded in a
              portfolio fact.


              Return JSON with this schema:

              {
                "subject_pt": "string (e-mail subject)",
                "greeting_pt": "string (e.g. Prezado Albert,)",
                "opening_pt": "string",
                "performance_pt": ["string (paragraphs)"],
                "macro_pt": "string",
                "suggestions_intro_pt": "string",
                "suggestions": [{"candidate_id": "string (copied)", "type": "opportunity|protection (copied)", "title_pt": "string", "text_pt": "string"}],
                "outlook_pt": "string",
                "closing_pt": "string",
                "charts": ["allocation|contribution|benchmarks", "allocation|contribution|benchmarks"]
              }


              ### Client

              {{client}}


              ### Client profile

              {{profile_summary}}


              ### Portfolio performance analysis

              {{performance_analysis}}


              ### XP macro digest

              {{macro_digest}}


